70. Code Block / Viewer

---

### 6️⃣ Navigation (71–80) — Hard

71. Navbar
72. Sidebar / Navigation Rail
73. Breadcrumbs
74. Pagination
75. Stepper / Wizard
76. Tabs Navigation
77. Mega Menu
78. Command Palette
79. Footer
80. App Switcher

---

### 7️⃣ Layout & Containers (81–88) — Hard

81. Responsive Grid
82. Container / Section
83. Split View
84. Resizable Panels
85. Sticky Header
86. Scroll Area
87. Masonry Layout
88. Dashboard Layout

---

### 8️⃣ Productivity & Workflow (89–95) — Hard

89. Kanban Board
90. Calendar (Month / Week / Day)
91. Scheduler (Resource-based)
92. Rich Text Editor
93. Comment System
94. Notification Center
95. Search Results Page Block

---

### 9️⃣ Enterprise & Platform Blocks (96–100) — Very Hard

96. Role & Permission Matrix
97. Audit Log Viewer
98. User Management Panel
99. Feature Flag Management UI
100. Workflow Builder / Rule Engine UI

---

## 5. Block Contract (Applies to ALL)

Every block must:

* Be headless-capable
* Expose state via attributes
* Support keyboard navigation
* Respect contrast & motion tokens
* Be composable, not closed

---

## 6. Difficulty Definition

* **Easy**: Pure UI, minimal state
* **Medium**: Local state + overlays
* **Hard**: Composition + coordination
* **Very Hard**: Domain logic + permissions

---

## 7. Enterprise Requirements

* RTL support
* Localization-ready
* Audit-safe interactions
* Predictable DOM
* No magic side effects

---

## 8. Success Metrics

* 100 blocks usable without customization
* 80% of enterprise screens built via composition
* Parity with React shadcn coverage
* Accessibility audits pass by default

---

## 9. Roadmap Recommendation

Phase 1 (MVP): Blocks 1–40
Phase 2 (Product): Blocks 41–80
Phase 3 (Enterprise): Blocks 81–100

---

## 10. Final Positioning Statement

> **shadcn-angular is not a component library — it is a complete UI building system, from primitive inputs to enterprise workflow engines.**

---

End of PRD
